# The input from which requirements.lock.txt (CPU) and requirements.lock.cu130.txt
# (GPU) are generated. It is NOT installed directly and NOT a lock.
#
# 38_clip's own files import torch, torchvision, numpy and PyYAML (those are
# requirements.txt); torchvision pulls Pillow transitively. This port also imports
# the pinned openai/CLIP `clip` package from third_party/CLIP, whose own runtime
# imports (ftfy, regex, tqdm, packaging; ftfy pulls wcwidth) must be installed for
# the import to succeed -- so they are listed here even though they are not this
# port's own imports and so are absent from requirements.txt. tqdm and packaging
# are pinned to the fleet's shared versions. Regenerate both locks from the
# repository root as for the other methods (uv pip compile against the fleet's
# shared pins, then bin/build-lock.py for the CPU lock; docs/GPU.md section 2).
torch
torchvision
numpy
PyYAML
ftfy
regex
tqdm
packaging
